---
// InternationalTaxComparison.astro
---
<div class="my-10 bg-navy-950 border border-navy-800 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-2xl">
  <div class="bg-navy-900 border-b border-navy-800 p-6 text-center">
    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white tracking-tight">The Global Fight Against Artificial Losses</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-navy-400 mt-1">Different jurisdictions, same underlying logic.</p>
  </div>
  
  <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 divide-y md:divide-y-0 md:divide-x divide-navy-800">
    
    <!-- United States -->
    <div class="p-6 sm:p-8 hover:bg-navy-900/50 transition-colors">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
        <div class="text-2xl">🇺🇸</div>
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white text-lg">United States</h4>
      </div>
      <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-emerald-500 font-bold mb-2">The Wash-Sale Rule</div>
      <p class="text-sm text-navy-300 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        If you sell a stock at a loss and buy a "substantially identical" stock within 30 days before or after, the loss is disallowed and added to the cost basis of the new stock.
      </p>
      <div class="bg-navy-900 border border-navy-700 rounded-lg p-3 text-xs text-navy-400 font-mono">
        IRS Publication 550
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- United Kingdom -->
    <div class="p-6 sm:p-8 hover:bg-navy-900/50 transition-colors">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
        <div class="text-2xl">🇬🇧</div>
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white text-lg">United Kingdom</h4>
      </div>
      <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-500 font-bold mb-2">Bed and Breakfasting</div>
      <p class="text-sm text-navy-300 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        If you sell shares and buy the same class of shares back within 30 days, the disposal is matched with the new acquisition rather than the original pool, killing the loss.
      </p>
      <div class="bg-navy-900 border border-navy-700 rounded-lg p-3 text-xs text-navy-400 font-mono">
        TCGA 1992, Section 106A
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- India -->
    <div class="p-6 sm:p-8 hover:bg-navy-900/50 transition-colors relative overflow-hidden group">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-br from-emerald-500/5 to-transparent z-0 pointer-events-none"></div>
      <div class="relative z-10">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
          <div class="text-2xl">🇮🇳</div>
          <h4 class="font-bold text-white text-lg">India</h4>
        </div>
        <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-emerald-500 font-bold mb-2">Section 94(7) & 94(8)</div>
        <p class="text-sm text-navy-300 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Targets corporate actions (dividends/bonuses) rather than market buys. Losses from selling original units are ignored and pushed to the cost basis of the retained units.
        </p>
        <div class="bg-emerald-500/10 border border-emerald-500/30 rounded-lg p-3 text-xs text-emerald-400 font-mono">
          Income Tax Act, 1961
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</div>
